==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|en|button-hole|button hole}}

===Etymology===
Originally {{m|en|buttonhold||a loop of string to hold a button down}}, but changed by [[folk etymology]] by influence of {{m|en|hole}}; see [[w:Folk_etymology|the Wikipedia article on folk etymology]]

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|en-us-buttonhole.ogg|a=US}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A [[hole]] through which a [[button]] is [[push]]ed to secure a garment or some part of one.
#: {{cot|en|eyelet|grommet}}
# {{lb|en|chiefly|British}} A [[flower]] worn in a buttonhole for decoration.
#: {{syn|en|boutonniere}}
## {{lb|en|attributive}} So shaped that it can be [[wear|worn]] on a buttonhole or it is similar to a buttonhole.
# {{senseid|en|surgery}} {{lb|en|surgery}} A small [[slot]]-like [[cut]] or [[incision]], made for example by an accident with the [[scalpel]].
#: {{cot|en|[[keyhole#English:_surgery|keyhole]]}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2011|author=George L. Spaeth; Helen Danesh-Meyer; Ivan Goldberg|title=Ophthalmic Surgery: Principles and Practice E-Book|page=220
|passage=The usual cause of conjunctival '''buttonholes''' is penetration of the tissue by the tip of a sharp instrument {{...}}}}
# The [[mouth]] and/or [[nose]] and/or [[eye]]s if appearing [[tiny]].<!--خَطْم-->
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} [[vagina]], [[coin slot]].
#: {{syn|en|Thesaurus:vagina}}
# {{senseid|en|anus}} {{lb|en|lightly|_|vulgar}} The [[butthole#English:_anus|butthole]] {{gloss|anus}}.
#: {{syn|en|Thesaurus:anus}}

